NDH‑Simulation‑Suite (“the Work”) is a conceptual physics and manifold‑architecture framework
designed for humane technology, research, accessibility, and high‑altitude systems thinking.
It is not a real‑world guidance system, weapons algorithm, or aerospace control stack.

This license preserves attribution, dignity invariants, and dual‑use safeguards while allowing
legitimate scientific, mathematical, and engineering exploration.

----------------------------------------------------------------------
1. PERMITTED USES
----------------------------------------------------------------------
You may:
• Study, extend, and transform the conceptual physics architecture.
• Use real physics, mathematics, and engineering transformations.
• Build research tools, simulations, educational materials, or humane systems.
• Create derivative works that preserve attribution, provenance, and NDH ethics membranes.

Real physics is allowed. Real engineering is allowed. Conceptual → operational mapping is allowed.
Weaponization is not.

----------------------------------------------------------------------
2. PROHIBITED USES (DUAL‑USE SAFEGUARD)
----------------------------------------------------------------------
The Work may not be used for:
• weapons development, targeting, guidance, or control;
• autonomous weapons systems or kinetic optimization;
• surveillance systems that violate human rights;
• any activity restricted under international arms‑control treaties, including:
    – Missile Technology Control Regime (MTCR),
    – Wassenaar Arrangement,
    – Hague Code of Conduct (HCoC),
    – and related dual‑use export‑control frameworks.

These references define ethical boundaries only. They are not operational guidance.

----------------------------------------------------------------------
3. ATTRIBUTION, PROVENANCE & DERIVATIVE DRIFT DISCLOSURE
----------------------------------------------------------------------
Derivative works must:
• preserve clear attribution to the original author;
• maintain provenance of NDH conceptual structures;
• disclose any reinterpretation of conceptual physics as real‑world physics;
• disclose any removal or modification of NDH ethical membranes;
• disclose any reframing of NDH primitives into operational algorithms.

Failure to disclose derivative drift constitutes a violation of this license.

